  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAL - Sustaining All Life</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201c;Healing the Roots, Caring for Life&#x201d; is a project that offers emotional support to climate activists, land defenders, and communities most affected by climate change. Using the listening circles methodology developed by Sustaining All Life, five young climate leaders will be trained to facilitate these circles within their own networks and beyond. The aim is to strengthen resilience, promote peer support, and reduce burnout, division, or dropout in climate and social justice movements. The project also includes mapping organisations that could benefit from emotional support to improve their advocacy and resilience. Through training, community meetings, and the creation of safe spaces, this initiative promotes community healing and the redistribution of care work&#x2014;especially among historically marginalised groups such as women, Indigenous peoples, migrants, youth, and LGBTIQ+ individuals. By centering care, the project lays the foundation for a more sustainable and inclusive climate movement.&#x201d;</narrative>
  </description>
